BLRP changes from upstream commit 9244b00dce5bb9956acb9999415e6537844fc42b:

1. Target net9.0/net9.0-windows so it can be built with the installed SDK.
2. Remove the stray standalone `W` in Views/SettingsWindow.xaml.cs.
3. Accept repeatable preview arguments in App.OnStartup:
   --preview <absolute-ydd-path> [--preview <absolute-ydd-path> ...]
   --gender <male|female>
4. In MainWindow_Loaded, import the requested YDDs into a dedicated outfit addon,
   select them together, navigate to the Project page, and open the 3D preview.
5. Bring the mandatory first-run setup window to the foreground so the splash
   screen cannot disappear while setup waits invisibly behind another window.
6. Listen on the PID-specific local named pipe
   `BLRP-grzyClothTool-outfit-<pid>` for later outfit preview requests.
7. Replace the dedicated outfit addon and preview later outfits in the existing
   window, restoring and activating it when necessary.
8. Resolve addon selection by collection position instead of parsing display
   names, so the generated BLRP outfit addon cannot crash the project window.
9. Avoid inserting the same drawable into SelectedDrawables twice while the
   preview selection changes.

The corresponding implementation is intentionally small and can be recreated
against the named upstream commit from this description.
